==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|вѣтвь||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|вѣтвь}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*větvь}}, {{m|sla-pro|*větь}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*wéh₁itis}}. Cognates include {{cog|bg|ве́тва}}, {{m|bg|ве́тка}}, {{m|bg|ве́я}}, and {{m|bg|ве́йка}}, {{cog/sl-tonal|vȇja}}, {{cog|cs|větev}}, {{cog|sk|vetva}}, {{cog|uk|ві́та}}. Non-Slavic cognates include {{cog|la|vītis|t=vine}}, {{cog|de|Weide|t=willow}}, {{cog|prg|witwan|t=willow}}, {{cog|fa|بید|tr=bid|t=willow}} and {{cog|en|withe}}.

